From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0088: the command thread instrument of P4 (submits,
 closes, transits, word waits, suspend points)

Chantier 48 P4.0, like 0071 for P0: counters in the perf overlay and the [perf] log, counted only while the
overlay is shown or --perf-log is set; no behaviour change.

- The submit cause in three: begin (pool commit, vkBeginCommandBuffer, timestamp harvest), end (marker,
  GuestSync post, vkEndCommandBuffer) and the time holding queue_mutex (vkQueueSubmit), per buffer.
- The frame close reason in four (suspend point, flip, CPU flip, wait flip done), and for every reason the
  closes of a buffer that recorded nothing; wait-flip-done closes with and without a pending flip request.
- Image::Transit calls by barrier or none, by path (whole image or per subresource) and by caller (targets,
  bindings, image heap, other), the calls with no barrier timed on a pseudo-random sample.
- Waits for GPU-written words: where the last writer stands (open buffer, submitted, executed), the buffers to
  it and after it, the share of the wait itself against the whole Finish().
- Suspend points: the delay from the game's enqueue to the command thread, then to the release, and the
  buffers on the GPU at both.
- The value-initialisation of DrawRenderState per draw, sampled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
